{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/409550-character-creation-help-for-newbie","id":409550,"title":"Character Creation help for Newbie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-17T20:34:40-08:00","id":409550,"title":"Character Creation help for Newbie","content":"I have just had an a-ha moment. HtV has been the one game that I just didn't get. The few times I have thumbed through the book it just seemed like a copy of D20 Modern. Now I have a character in mind that I feel is probably perfect for the game. The original idea was to have a guy that just wanders into Arcadia through curiosity. Gets involved with the Mechanical Forest (Winter Masques pg. 148). He gives it his all to become a part of it all, and discovers that instead of being inspired by role-models, he was anti-inspired by anti-role-models. The ones that were the most successful in the Mechanical Forest were the exact antithesis of what he himself wanted to become. The period of time he spent there didn't really change him much and he discovered, exploits if you will on how to destroy the Mechanical Forest. It was all based on the denizens' inability to change or adapt. He didn't have to escape from Arcadia he was sent back to the mortal world for what the Fae considered incompetence.<br /> <br /> Here is where the dilema hit. Started as a Darkling Antiquarian with the pure inability or desire to raise his Wryd. The problem is that in the game Changeling the Lost, power is gained by increasing Wryd and contracts. Then I decided that I actually don't have a Changeling at all, but rather a human with a secret how to kick the Faes' ass in Arcadia. That is a Hunter, a mortal that hunts down all of nWOD's supernatural creatures. Is there one of the HtV supplement books that covers how a mortal deals with the hedge, hobgoblins and the Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","user":"Thinking_Point","date":". 02-17-2015, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","name":"Thinking_Point","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:18:18-08:00","id":411450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thinking_Point</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/409550-character-creation-help-for-newbie#post409550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there one of the HtV supplement books that covers how a mortal deals with the hedge, hobgoblins and the Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Purchase <b>Mortal Remains</b>. Now.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custo